(2754782, 382783, 43463, '<td valign="top">I can see what you tried to accomplish in this photo. There are ''numerous'' mysterious ghostly figures milling about. The problem is the composition and angle. None of the figures are terribly prominent in the photo. The figures in the distance maybe make-up 4 % of the photo. While those in the foreground are almost not visible because they blend into the dark background and the busy lights of the city. Making those ghostly figures in the foreground more prominent would be the key to moving this out of the average range and into the 7 and up range. Perhaps shooting the photo at a lower angle would have helped. Placing the camera low to the ground and shooting angled up so that the figures appear more on the backdrop of the blue sky would have made them as visible as those ghostly figures you see in the background faintly silhouetted on the ocean. Also too much of the bright lights would only serve to distract attention away from one of the key elements that being the ghostly figures. Just keeping a narrow slice of the city lights and city line  would help keep the atttention tihtly focused on the main elements and make a stronger connection to the title of the piece.</td>', 'I can see what you tried to accomplish in this photo. There are ''numerous'' mysterious ghostly figures milling about. The problem is the composition and angle. None of the figures are terribly prominent in the photo. The figures in the distance maybe make-up 4 % of the photo. While those in the foreground are almost not visible because they blend into the dark background and the busy lights of the city. Making those ghostly figures in the foreground more prominent would be the key to moving this out of the average range and into the 7 and up range. Perhaps shooting the photo at a lower angle would have helped. Placing the camera low to the ground and shooting angled up so that the figures appear more on the backdrop of the blue sky would have made them as visible as those ghostly figures you see in the background faintly silhouetted on the ocean. Also too much of the bright lights would only serve to distract attention away from one of the key elements that being the ghostly figures. Just keeping a narrow slice of the city lights and city line  would help keep the atttention tihtly focused on the main elements and make a stronger connection to the title of the piece.', '2006-08-23 22:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754903, 383007, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing image.  You did a great job "painting" the star around the man''s head and making him seem to float in the air.  8.</td>', 'This is an amazing image.  You did a great job "painting" the star around the man''s head and making him seem to float in the air.  8.', '2006-08-23 23:15:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754908, 382804, 43463, '<td valign="top">Certainly a different take on Magic &amp; Mystery. A tribute to those of us who still love mysteries - and who grew up on Nancy Drew or the Hardy Boys:-) My first Nancy Drew that I read was #47 The Mysterious Stranger - then I read all of them...but I digress. The merits and critique on the photo. I was going to make the point that the model should have had her hair like Nancy''s seen on the back cover when it then dawned on me that the title plays into the reason. She is wearing pigtails which is a connection to childhood - and even though us gals get old we always remember our girlhood reading and enjoying Nancy Drew. The expression of the model is good because it shows she is totally engrossed in the action that is happening in the pages of the book. My critiques lie in the elements of the composition. I think that if the pigtails stuck out more than an even stronger connection to childhood and you are never too old would be established. I also think that you could have better utilized the background space - here it is just negative space that has nothing in it. It could have been used to help make a stronger connection to the enjoyment of reading Nancy Drew. Some examples: the cover art for The Mysterious Mannequin shows a veiled woman pointing to a tapestry. You could have had that book in the shot and had a tapestry similiar to the cover art hanging in the background. Or the cover art for The Clue In The Old Album you could have had a picture of a moustached man playing a violin hanging in the background to match the book cover. Or The Scarlet Slipper Mystery in which you have a painting of a ballerina in the background to match the cover art of the book.....you see where I am going with the suggestion. If there is some negative space in the shot that can be used to strengthen an element in the shot without it becoming too busy then it might be worth exploring. Lastly, mayhap tis just me, but the green shirt just is too overpowering a tone for the photo. A more muted green......mayhap even clothes that alludes to an elementry school uniform or girl scouts uniform would have would have been better for the composition for it would help strengthen the connection  to childhood and one "never being too old" to enjoy a revisit to an "old friend"</td>', 'Certainly a different take on Magic & Mystery. A tribute to those of us who still love mysteries - and who grew up on Nancy Drew or the Hardy Boys:-) My first Nancy Drew that I read was #47 The Mysterious Stranger - then I read all of them...but I digress. The merits and critique on the photo. I was going to make the point that the model should have had her hair like Nancy''s seen on the back cover when it then dawned on me that the title plays into the reason. She is wearing pigtails which is a connection to childhood - and even though us gals get old we always remember our girlhood reading and enjoying Nancy Drew. The expression of the model is good because it shows she is totally engrossed in the action that is happening in the pages of the book. My critiques lie in the elements of the composition. I think that if the pigtails stuck out more than an even stronger connection to childhood and you are never too old would be established. I also think that you could have better utilized the background space - here it is just negative space that has nothing in it. It could have been used to help make a stronger connection to the enjoyment of reading Nancy Drew. Some examples: the cover art for The Mysterious Mannequin shows a veiled woman pointing to a tapestry. You could have had that book in the shot and had a tapestry similiar to the cover art hanging in the background. Or the cover art for The Clue In The Old Album you could have had a picture of a moustached man playing a violin hanging in the background to match the book cover. Or The Scarlet Slipper Mystery in which you have a painting of a ballerina in the background to match the cover art of the book.....you see where I am going with the suggestion. If there is some negative space in the shot that can be used to strengthen an element in the shot without it becoming too busy then it might be worth exploring. Lastly, mayhap tis just me, but the green shirt just is too overpowering a tone for the photo. A more muted green......mayhap even clothes that alludes to an elementry school uniform or girl scouts uniform would have would have been better for the composition for it would help strengthen the connection  to childhood and one "never being too old" to enjoy a revisit to an "old friend"', '2006-08-23 23:16:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754916, 382667, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot.  The soft focus works well here.  Her skin tones contrasts beautifully with the dark leaves around her.  I also like how her face and hair fade smoothly into the darkness around her face.  8.</td>', 'I like this shot a lot.  The soft focus works well here.  Her skin tones contrasts beautifully with the dark leaves around her.  I also like how her face and hair fade smoothly into the darkness around her face.  8.', '2006-08-23 23:18:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754918, 382971, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is really wonderful.  I like how wide-set the eyes are.  The dog''s left eye (picture right) is a little blurry, but that''s okay.  7!</td>', 'This is really wonderful.  I like how wide-set the eyes are.  The dog''s left eye (picture right) is a little blurry, but that''s okay.  7!', '2006-08-23 23:18:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754926, 382444, 60862, '<td valign="top">I liked all of the levitation images, but this was the best.  The intensity of his gaze is something else, and I like how you got his eye into the same space with the floating object.  I hope you share how you did it. 8.</td>', 'I liked all of the levitation images, but this was the best.  The intensity of his gaze is something else, and I like how you got his eye into the same space with the floating object.  I hope you share how you did it. 8.', '2006-08-23 23:20:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754927, 382866, 60862, '<td valign="top">Neat image!  All of the elements come together nicely - the off-center magnifying glass, the fingerprints, and the diagonal of the knife.  The blacklight also adds a modern touch.  And the bright contrasts great with the dim blue.  7.</td>', 'Neat image!  All of the elements come together nicely - the off-center magnifying glass, the fingerprints, and the diagonal of the knife.  The blacklight also adds a modern touch.  And the bright contrasts great with the dim blue.  7.', '2006-08-23 23:21:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754933, 381904, 60862, '<td valign="top">A touch of whimsy to go with the mystery.  I like how bright his green eyes are and how you put him over on the right.  Minor nitpick is I would''ve liked to have seen his entire hat.  6.</td>', 'A touch of whimsy to go with the mystery.  I like how bright his green eyes are and how you put him over on the right.  Minor nitpick is I would''ve liked to have seen his entire hat.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:22:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754939, 382758, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is a nice image, and I got the mystery angle immediately from the image.  The title is a bit heavy-handed for me;  I prefer titles to be icing on the cake, not the tool to explain why the image fits.  Just one opinion, of course ... 6.</td>', 'This is a nice image, and I got the mystery angle immediately from the image.  The title is a bit heavy-handed for me;  I prefer titles to be icing on the cake, not the tool to explain why the image fits.  Just one opinion, of course ... 6.', '2006-08-23 23:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754941, 383048, 60862, '<td valign="top">Who is she?  Why is she sad?  What''s she thinking?  The colors and composition are very nice.  Selective desat works for me in this image. 6.</td>', 'Who is she?  Why is she sad?  What''s she thinking?  The colors and composition are very nice.  Selective desat works for me in this image. 6.', '2006-08-23 23:24:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754949, 382810, 60862, '<td valign="top">The color here, or more specifically lack thereof, adds a nice street feeling to the image for me.  His intense concentration is interesting to see.  My only concern is that the woman with her arms folded is distracting, even though you did a nice job of blurring out the audience.  Perhaps a different crop would help with that?  6.</td>', 'The color here, or more specifically lack thereof, adds a nice street feeling to the image for me.  His intense concentration is interesting to see.  My only concern is that the woman with her arms folded is distracting, even though you did a nice job of blurring out the audience.  Perhaps a different crop would help with that?  6.', '2006-08-23 23:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754952, 383040, 60862, '<td valign="top">Who is that?  What''s she doing?  Why?  Nice image!  The off-center position is interesting here, along with the partial reflection.  The stormy sky adds an air of mystery.  6.</td>', 'Who is that?  What''s she doing?  Why?  Nice image!  The off-center position is interesting here, along with the partial reflection.  The stormy sky adds an air of mystery.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:27:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754957, 382858, 60862, '<td valign="top">Spooky!  I like it a lot.  The soft focus works well in this case. I like the tight crop - it emphasizes her face over her hair and keeps the focus on her eyes.  6.</td>', 'Spooky!  I like it a lot.  The soft focus works well in this case. I like the tight crop - it emphasizes her face over her hair and keeps the focus on her eyes.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:27:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754959, 382470, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like this better than the other northern lights shot because it has more context.  I can imagine the glow as a magical spell here, maybe from a passing wizard or witch.  I also love night shots that incorporate stars. 6.</td>', 'I like this better than the other northern lights shot because it has more context.  I can imagine the glow as a magical spell here, maybe from a passing wizard or witch.  I also love night shots that incorporate stars. 6.', '2006-08-23 23:28:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754965, 383047, 60862, '<td valign="top">Very cute concept.  The cat''s expression is wonderful.  She looks as surprised as the title indicates the magician is feeling.  The negative space at the top makes me think she''s about to leap out of there as quickly as she can.  6.</td>', 'Very cute concept.  The cat''s expression is wonderful.  She looks as surprised as the title indicates the magician is feeling.  The negative space at the top makes me think she''s about to leap out of there as quickly as she can.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:29:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2754983, 383042, 43463, '<td valign="top">:spoken with a british chimney sweep accent: Oh, I know that silhouette anywhere - Mary Poppins!!!:-)This is a wonderful shot trying to capture the magic of Mary Poppins. I love the silhouette of the woman against a blueish grey sky. The vast negative space works for it keeps the eye''s attention on the main focus/element of the composition. With the hat, the umbrella, and the overcoat she does take on the impression of Mary Poppins but there are two little things that could have strengthened the connection to the charming mysterious Mary Poppins even more (I know picky picky, but spit-spot lets have a look into it shall we?;-) ).  The Mary Poppins we are all familiar with and love is that brought about by Julie Andrews performance. She always made it a point to stand with her toes sticking out and heels together because she wanted to remain true to the illustrations in P.L. Travers Mary Poppins books. Also, there is the flower that sticks up out of her hat and I see no adornment on this figure. Lastly the pose of the model seems a tad stiff. Her movements seem forced in this photo as that the arm with the bag is lifted much too high and the arm sporting the umbrella seems held too stiff - I would imagine that the arm holding the umbrella would be holding much more aloft in order to catch a breeze to take flight.</td>', ':spoken with a british chimney sweep accent: Oh, I know that silhouette anywhere - Mary Poppins!!!:-)This is a wonderful shot trying to capture the magic of Mary Poppins. I love the silhouette of the woman against a blueish grey sky. The vast negative space works for it keeps the eye''s attention on the main focus/element of the composition. With the hat, the umbrella, and the overcoat she does take on the impression of Mary Poppins but there are two little things that could have strengthened the connection to the charming mysterious Mary Poppins even more (I know picky picky, but spit-spot lets have a look into it shall we?;-) ).  The Mary Poppins we are all familiar with and love is that brought about by Julie Andrews performance. She always made it a point to stand with her toes sticking out and heels together because she wanted to remain true to the illustrations in P.L. Travers Mary Poppins books. Also, there is the flower that sticks up out of her hat and I see no adornment on this figure. Lastly the pose of the model seems a tad stiff. Her movements seem forced in this photo as that the arm with the bag is lifted much too high and the arm sporting the umbrella seems held too stiff - I would imagine that the arm holding the umbrella would be holding much more aloft in order to catch a breeze to take flight.', '2006-08-23 23:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755003, 382635, 60862, '<td valign="top">Interesting angle and nice idea with the floating feather.  The models'' expressions work, too, and sell the idea that it''s magical.  Not sure about the tight crop on the left and empty space on the right.  6.</td>', 'Interesting angle and nice idea with the floating feather.  The models'' expressions work, too, and sell the idea that it''s magical.  Not sure about the tight crop on the left and empty space on the right.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755011, 383046, 60862, '<td valign="top">I started out with a 6 for this, but I''m upping it to an 8.  It really captures the challenge topic perfectly, and it''s a great image on top of that.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I like how the hands are lit enough to know what they are without dominating the picture, and how the fingers curl to lead my eye back to the flame spiral.   Very nice!</td>', 'I started out with a 6 for this, but I''m upping it to an 8.  It really captures the challenge topic perfectly, and it''s a great image on top of that.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I like how the hands are lit enough to know what they are without dominating the picture, and how the fingers curl to lead my eye back to the flame spiral.   Very nice!', '2006-08-23 23:38:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755022, 382687, 60862, '<td valign="top">Luckily, the title made me look closer to see that she''s kissing a frog.  But I almost missed it entirely, and just saw a cute girl dressed like a princess.  Normally I don''t like titles to tell me the story;  I prefer that in the image.<br/> <br/>But the rest of the image is so nice - the contrast between her coloring and that of her dress against the brown background, her expression, her gorgeous eyes ... and I like the soft focus.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, the large empty space on the left doesn''t do much for me.<br/> <br/>With a tighter crop and maybe her hand lower so I could really see the frog, I would''ve voted higher.  Still, I''m voting it a 6.</td>', 'Luckily, the title made me look closer to see that she''s kissing a frog.  But I almost missed it entirely, and just saw a cute girl dressed like a princess.  Normally I don''t like titles to tell me the story;  I prefer that in the image. But the rest of the image is so nice - the contrast between her coloring and that of her dress against the brown background, her expression, her gorgeous eyes ... and I like the soft focus. Compositionally, the large empty space on the left doesn''t do much for me. With a tighter crop and maybe her hand lower so I could really see the frog, I would''ve voted higher.  Still, I''m voting it a 6.', '2006-08-23 23:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755023, 382807, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.  Clean, no wasted space, lit well.  Only nitpick would be to have the hand sharper. Could be one of those inspirational posters.  6.</td>', 'Nicely done.  Clean, no wasted space, lit well.  Only nitpick would be to have the hand sharper. Could be one of those inspirational posters.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:42:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755026, 382878, 60862, '<td valign="top">Started out at 6, upping it to 7.  Creepy, and the spirit soaring out of the skull really drives home the magical feel.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  The moon also adds a nice touch.  7.</td>', 'Started out at 6, upping it to 7.  Creepy, and the spirit soaring out of the skull really drives home the magical feel.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  The moon also adds a nice touch.  7.', '2006-08-23 23:43:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755031, 383041, 60862, '<td valign="top">I really like this one.  The expression on her face is terrific!  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I also like the lighting - it''s dramatic on her face.<br/> <br/>A nitpick would be to clean up the bumpiness in the wall.  You did a nice job of fuzzing it out on the left around her head, so I mean to extend that to the left edge and also from the right side of her head to the right edge.<br/> <br/>6.</td>', 'I really like this one.  The expression on her face is terrific!  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I also like the lighting - it''s dramatic on her face. A nitpick would be to clean up the bumpiness in the wall.  You did a nice job of fuzzing it out on the left around her head, so I mean to extend that to the left edge and also from the right side of her head to the right edge. 6.', '2006-08-23 23:45:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755035, 382939, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ha!  I thought about trying this for the rope challenge.<br/> <br/>Your actors did a nice job selling it with their expressions, and I love the kid pointing it out to someone off-camera (an adult, maybe?). 6.</td>', 'Ha!  I thought about trying this for the rope challenge. Your actors did a nice job selling it with their expressions, and I love the kid pointing it out to someone off-camera (an adult, maybe?). 6.', '2006-08-23 23:47:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755036, 382748, 43463, '<td valign="top">Ack!! My what an interesting eye you have - both the pepper and the photographer who imagined this concept:-) Definatly an unusual and interesting take on the mystery portion of the challenge - gotta give you points for creativity. Certainly mysterious and downright erie. One certainly does not expect to see an eye staring back at them from the stalk of a green pepper. A slightly above average shot - lighting and concept are great. There are some improvements that could be made to some of the compositional elements to make it more appealing. First the background color is too much of a screaming neon tone that IMHO takes focus and attention away from the main subject because most are shielding their eyes from the brightness of the hue. Next the condition of the green pepper looks like it has faired better days. A fresher, healther green pepper with a more robust green hue would add to improving the visual appeal of the composition.</td>', 'Ack!! My what an interesting eye you have - both the pepper and the photographer who imagined this concept:-) Definatly an unusual and interesting take on the mystery portion of the challenge - gotta give you points for creativity. Certainly mysterious and downright erie. One certainly does not expect to see an eye staring back at them from the stalk of a green pepper. A slightly above average shot - lighting and concept are great. There are some improvements that could be made to some of the compositional elements to make it more appealing. First the background color is too much of a screaming neon tone that IMHO takes focus and attention away from the main subject because most are shielding their eyes from the brightness of the hue. Next the condition of the green pepper looks like it has faired better days. A fresher, healther green pepper with a more robust green hue would add to improving the visual appeal of the composition.', '2006-08-23 23:47:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755039, 382636, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice!   The lighting works well on the gloves, and the hands and bulb are placed very well.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  Bumping from 6 to 7.</td>', 'Nice!   The lighting works well on the gloves, and the hands and bulb are placed very well.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  Bumping from 6 to 7.', '2006-08-23 23:48:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755040, 381734, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  I like how you placed the note - not too perfectly, but clearly in the light so we can read it. I might''ve cropped it tigher at the top - that black space doesn''t add anything for me.  But the hand is terrific.  6.</td>', 'Nice idea.  I like how you placed the note - not too perfectly, but clearly in the light so we can read it. I might''ve cropped it tigher at the top - that black space doesn''t add anything for me.  But the hand is terrific.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:48:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755044, 381952, 60862, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I like how you blurred her face - that emphasizes her hand and the floating pencil.  And her face, hand, and pencil are placed well.<br/> <br/>The blue tint to the girl detracts from it for me, but still, a 6.</td>', 'Very nice shot.  I look forward to reading how you did it.  I like how you blurred her face - that emphasizes her hand and the floating pencil.  And her face, hand, and pencil are placed well. The blue tint to the girl detracts from it for me, but still, a 6.', '2006-08-23 23:50:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755046, 381445, 60862, '<td valign="top">LOL.  Unlike many other entries, I got the mystery of this one even without the title! Not much to say about it - sometimes you get lucky with what you see, and you shoot.  You framed the tiger nicely within his cave.  6.</td>', 'LOL.  Unlike many other entries, I got the mystery of this one even without the title! Not much to say about it - sometimes you get lucky with what you see, and you shoot.  You framed the tiger nicely within his cave.  6.', '2006-08-23 23:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755049, 383053, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice!  I like the composition and the lighting, especially how the shadow dominates the upper left corner. 6.</td>', 'Nice!  I like the composition and the lighting, especially how the shadow dominates the upper left corner. 6.', '2006-08-23 23:51:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755055, 382589, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like how you blurred the hands to put the emphasis on the cards.  I also like how they fan out - it''s a nice shape.  This is a good example of how centering the objects can work well.  How''d you do it?  6.</td>', 'I like how you blurred the hands to put the emphasis on the cards.  I also like how they fan out - it''s a nice shape.  This is a good example of how centering the objects can work well.  How''d you do it?  6.', '2006-08-23 23:53:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755056, 382748, 60862, '<td valign="top">Funny.  The mystery here strikes me as wondering whose eye that is!  Or is the stem really a periscope for some tiny explorer?  I do like the pepper on the left edge - gives some where for the eye to peer into, but maybe I''d like it better if the negative space were a little smaller.  5.</td>', 'Funny.  The mystery here strikes me as wondering whose eye that is!  Or is the stem really a periscope for some tiny explorer?  I do like the pepper on the left edge - gives some where for the eye to peer into, but maybe I''d like it better if the negative space were a little smaller.  5.', '2006-08-23 23:53:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755057, 382722, 60862, '<td valign="top">Interesting.  To me, I get "enchanted forest with maybe a witch''s cottage in it."  So the title doesn''t mesh with the image for me.  Not counting against it for that reason, just mentioning it.  As for the image, as I said, it does evoke magic, but not strongly, and the colors are so muted as to not really grab me.  Just my opinion, of course. 5.</td>', 'Interesting.  To me, I get "enchanted forest with maybe a witch''s cottage in it."  So the title doesn''t mesh with the image for me.  Not counting against it for that reason, just mentioning it.  As for the image, as I said, it does evoke magic, but not strongly, and the colors are so muted as to not really grab me.  Just my opinion, of course. 5.', '2006-08-23 23:53:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755058, 382136, 60862, '<td valign="top">This image meets the challenge, because I can see it''s somehow about magic, so I start with a 5.  Her expression is funny, but a little blurry, and I don''t really understand how the orange ball relates to her expression or the newt.  I tend to prefer titles that are icing on the cake and have the image tell the story, and even with the title, it''s missing something for me.  I do like the composition - her face, the ball, and the newt are in good positions.  5.</td>', 'This image meets the challenge, because I can see it''s somehow about magic, so I start with a 5.  Her expression is funny, but a little blurry, and I don''t really understand how the orange ball relates to her expression or the newt.  I tend to prefer titles that are icing on the cake and have the image tell the story, and even with the title, it''s missing something for me.  I do like the composition - her face, the ball, and the newt are in good positions.  5.', '2006-08-23 23:53:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755067, 382646, 60862, '<td valign="top">I originally gave this a 5 because the image didn''t convey magic or mystery to me, but it''s a nice shot nonetheless.  And I usually expect the picture to tell the story, with the title as icing on the cake.  However, here the title got me to broaden my perspective (esp. since I have two young daughters!).<br/> <br/>Now, looking at the photo itself, I like the lighting, how you placed the baby and the dad''s face, and of course the baby''s expression!  B&amp;W works nicely, too.<br/> <br/>6.</td>', 'I originally gave this a 5 because the image didn''t convey magic or mystery to me, but it''s a nice shot nonetheless.  And I usually expect the picture to tell the story, with the title as icing on the cake.  However, here the title got me to broaden my perspective (esp. since I have two young daughters!). Now, looking at the photo itself, I like the lighting, how you placed the baby and the dad''s face, and of course the baby''s expression!  B&W works nicely, too. 6.', '2006-08-23 23:55:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755070, 382468, 60862, '<td valign="top">It clearly meets the challenge, which for me starts it at 5.<br/> <br/>However, this is a pretty dead-on take on some magic tricks.  Nothing too dramatic about the layout or the lighting (which is flat).  Try playing with lights next time to create some shadows or try a lower angle.<br/> <br/>It''s reasonably sharp and decently lit, though, so it''s still a 5.</td>', 'It clearly meets the challenge, which for me starts it at 5. However, this is a pretty dead-on take on some magic tricks.  Nothing too dramatic about the layout or the lighting (which is flat).  Try playing with lights next time to create some shadows or try a lower angle. It''s reasonably sharp and decently lit, though, so it''s still a 5.', '2006-08-23 23:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755073, 381856, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the elements in the photo, but it''s not an especially dramatic presentation.  Stronger lighting from one side, with some shadows, might help, or maybe a different angle.  5.</td>', 'I like the elements in the photo, but it''s not an especially dramatic presentation.  Stronger lighting from one side, with some shadows, might help, or maybe a different angle.  5.', '2006-08-23 23:57:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755088, 381724, 60862, '<td valign="top">It meets the challenge in that unicorns are magical.  But the image itself doesn''t really grab me.  Maybe if the clouds had been sharp?  5.</td>', 'It meets the challenge in that unicorns are magical.  But the image itself doesn''t really grab me.  Maybe if the clouds had been sharp?  5.', '2006-08-24 00:00:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755096, 382918, 60862, '<td valign="top">I understand that with your title you mean magic light for photographers, but that''s too narrow for me in this challenge.  It''s a very pretty sunset or sunrise, but not especially strong in the magic or mystery.  5.</td>', 'I understand that with your title you mean magic light for photographers, but that''s too narrow for me in this challenge.  It''s a very pretty sunset or sunrise, but not especially strong in the magic or mystery.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:01:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755100, 383042, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the concept a lot.  Something''s just missing for me.  Maybe the cloudy sky isn''t interesting enough, or maybe it''s that "Mary" seems rooted to the ground.  Even a little air under her would''ve added a lot.  5.</td>', 'I like the concept a lot.  Something''s just missing for me.  Maybe the cloudy sky isn''t interesting enough, or maybe it''s that "Mary" seems rooted to the ground.  Even a little air under her would''ve added a lot.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755108, 382098, 60862, '<td valign="top">I''ll give you that the forest appears dark and mysterious here.  But the composition and silhouettes of the trees don''t grab me.  I''m sorry I can''t be more specific, but that''s the case with a lot of images I rate as a 5, which I''m doing here.  To me, that means it meets the challenge and it''s a decent shot, but it''s not really great.  5.</td>', 'I''ll give you that the forest appears dark and mysterious here.  But the composition and silhouettes of the trees don''t grab me.  I''m sorry I can''t be more specific, but that''s the case with a lot of images I rate as a 5, which I''m doing here.  To me, that means it meets the challenge and it''s a decent shot, but it''s not really great.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:04:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755111, 382968, 60862, '<td valign="top">Assuming this is a cutout, something about it doesn''t yield a believable image to me.  Maybe it''s how she''s not as sharp as her surroundings, or that she''s brighter than the rest of the hole she''s in.  I like the concept a lot, but the execution isn''t there.  5.<br/> <br/>It''s interesting to me it was validated.  I wonder what made someone think this wasn''t legit?</td>', 'Assuming this is a cutout, something about it doesn''t yield a believable image to me.  Maybe it''s how she''s not as sharp as her surroundings, or that she''s brighter than the rest of the hole she''s in.  I like the concept a lot, but the execution isn''t there.  5. It''s interesting to me it was validated.  I wonder what made someone think this wasn''t legit?', '2006-08-24 00:06:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755120, 382877, 60862, '<td valign="top">Like the other sunset shots, I think they''re pretty without really evoking magic for me.   I do like the reflection - makes the water very dramatic.  5.</td>', 'Like the other sunset shots, I think they''re pretty without really evoking magic for me.   I do like the reflection - makes the water very dramatic.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:10:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755122, 381101, 60862, '<td valign="top">Like the other sunset shots, I think they''re pretty without really evoking magic for me.   This one''s more dramatic than the others, though.  5.</td>', 'Like the other sunset shots, I think they''re pretty without really evoking magic for me.   This one''s more dramatic than the others, though.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:11:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755129, 382712, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the idea here.  The orange works well in contrast to the cat''s black.  In fact, it works a little too well, such that I can barely see the cat beyond his eyes (my monitor''s brightness is turned all the way up, too).  But the composition is good.  6.</td>', 'I like the idea here.  The orange works well in contrast to the cat''s black.  In fact, it works a little too well, such that I can barely see the cat beyond his eyes (my monitor''s brightness is turned all the way up, too).  But the composition is good.  6.', '2006-08-24 00:12:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755132, 382240, 60862, '<td valign="top">The idea is interesting, but something about the pose and cropping makes me think of someone lying on a bed instead of hovering mid-air.  Aside from that, though, I like the composition an use of B&amp;W.<br/> <br/>I don''t usually notice borders or comment on them, but this one bothers me.  I feel like I want to see more here, and the border on the right frustrates me.  5.</td>', 'The idea is interesting, but something about the pose and cropping makes me think of someone lying on a bed instead of hovering mid-air.  Aside from that, though, I like the composition an use of B&W. I don''t usually notice borders or comment on them, but this one bothers me.  I feel like I want to see more here, and the border on the right frustrates me.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:14:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755143, 382431, 60862, '<td valign="top">Interesting shapes, but I get only a weak sense of mystery here.  I do like how they make a diagonal line across the photo, and the cloudy sky adds drama.  In fact, it''s an interesting image outside of this challenge. <br/> <br/>Giving you the benefit of the doubt, I''ll assume you saw this and thought "warlock" or "magic," but to me, they''re just dramatic, interesting shapes.  Be careful what you assume will resonate with others.  Of course, having said that, you''ll probably get a high 6 or 7. :)<br/> <br/>But from me, 5.</td>', 'Interesting shapes, but I get only a weak sense of mystery here.  I do like how they make a diagonal line across the photo, and the cloudy sky adds drama.  In fact, it''s an interesting image outside of this challenge.  Giving you the benefit of the doubt, I''ll assume you saw this and thought "warlock" or "magic," but to me, they''re just dramatic, interesting shapes.  Be careful what you assume will resonate with others.  Of course, having said that, you''ll probably get a high 6 or 7. :) But from me, 5.', '2006-08-24 00:17:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755151, 382388, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the concept, and to me, it clearly meets the challenge.<br/> <br/>The green glow is nice, but I think the cropping hurts it.  If there were some black space around it to convey an empty room where something interesting was going on in this trunk, that''s grab me more.<br/> <br/>Instead, the close cropping reduces the drama and puts my attention on niggling things like lack of focus and wondering what''s being hidden in the corners of the lid by the blown highlights.  5.</td>', 'I like the concept, and to me, it clearly meets the challenge. The green glow is nice, but I think the cropping hurts it.  If there were some black space around it to convey an empty room where something interesting was going on in this trunk, that''s grab me more. Instead, the close cropping reduces the drama and puts my attention on niggling things like lack of focus and wondering what''s being hidden in the corners of the lid by the blown highlights.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:19:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755160, 382151, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is a tough image for me.  On the one hand, I love the concept, the hand is well-lit and sharp, and the flame looks nice.<br/> <br/>On the other hand, aside from the literal placement of the flame, there doesn''t seem to be much connection to the hand.  I''m looking for something that''s burning, and I find myself wondering whether this is a reflection instead of just being absorbed by the photo.  I''m sorry I don''t have anything more specific to give you.  5.</td>', 'This is a tough image for me.  On the one hand, I love the concept, the hand is well-lit and sharp, and the flame looks nice. On the other hand, aside from the literal placement of the flame, there doesn''t seem to be much connection to the hand.  I''m looking for something that''s burning, and I find myself wondering whether this is a reflection instead of just being absorbed by the photo.  I''m sorry I don''t have anything more specific to give you.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:21:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755162, 382663, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the placement of the main trunk and the branches, and I like the soft focus - it adds to the fantasy feel.  I feel like something''s missing, though - maybe a stronger subject?  Still, I''m bumping it from a 5 to a 6.</td>', 'I like the placement of the main trunk and the branches, and I like the soft focus - it adds to the fantasy feel.  I feel like something''s missing, though - maybe a stronger subject?  Still, I''m bumping it from a 5 to a 6.', '2006-08-24 00:22:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755170, 382804, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the concept, and I like the picture, but it doesn''t especially grab me.<br/> <br/>Decent photo that meets the challenge is what I vote as a 5.<br/> <br/>I''m sorry I don''t have anything to suggest.  I like the composition, but maybe there''s no way to take this particular concept that would really grab me.  Maybe having the book glow?  5.</td>', 'I like the concept, and I like the picture, but it doesn''t especially grab me. Decent photo that meets the challenge is what I vote as a 5. I''m sorry I don''t have anything to suggest.  I like the composition, but maybe there''s no way to take this particular concept that would really grab me.  Maybe having the book glow?  5.', '2006-08-24 00:26:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755176, 382414, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the concept (I know what dreamcatchers are), the placement within the frame, and the bokeh (blurred background).  Maybe with a little brighter lighting I''d have voted this higher.  5.</td>', 'I like the concept (I know what dreamcatchers are), the placement within the frame, and the bokeh (blurred background).  Maybe with a little brighter lighting I''d have voted this higher.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:29:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755186, 383015, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the concept, the glowing ball, and the composition.<br/> <br/>Her face is too dim for me, though, so it doesn''t draw me in as much as I''d like.  Decent shots that meet the challenge define 5 for me, so 5 it is.</td>', 'I like the concept, the glowing ball, and the composition. Her face is too dim for me, though, so it doesn''t draw me in as much as I''d like.  Decent shots that meet the challenge define 5 for me, so 5 it is.', '2006-08-24 00:31:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755191, 382990, 60862, '<td valign="top">I get the mystery of who he is, but the title leaves me cold.  Compositionally, I would''ve liked less board.  Not really more of him, but less board.  Maybe even cutting the picture in half horizontally and showing the top half, with him peeking out.  The shot is also very soft in focus;  sharpness in his face would add a lot to his expression.  And the lighting is pretty dim.  All in all, I''m on the fence but I''ll give it a minor bump to 5.</td>', 'I get the mystery of who he is, but the title leaves me cold.  Compositionally, I would''ve liked less board.  Not really more of him, but less board.  Maybe even cutting the picture in half horizontally and showing the top half, with him peeking out.  The shot is also very soft in focus;  sharpness in his face would add a lot to his expression.  And the lighting is pretty dim.  All in all, I''m on the fence but I''ll give it a minor bump to 5.', '2006-08-24 00:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755192, 382603, 60862, '<td valign="top">Mystery and magic in one shot.  I guess I would''ve liked to see more of the magician, though.  The rest of it is so dark and green that a stronger subject would improve it.  Still, a 5.</td>', 'Mystery and magic in one shot.  I guess I would''ve liked to see more of the magician, though.  The rest of it is so dark and green that a stronger subject would improve it.  Still, a 5.', '2006-08-24 00:35:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755197, 382781, 60862, '<td valign="top">Okay, it''s a magic trick.  Challenge met.<br/> <br/>The magnifying glass in this case doesn''t add anything for me.  I initially thought it would show me something like how the cards are marked, but instead it seems like it was just added to add it or to explore how such lenses behave in photos.  5.</td>', 'Okay, it''s a magic trick.  Challenge met. The magnifying glass in this case doesn''t add anything for me.  I initially thought it would show me something like how the cards are marked, but instead it seems like it was just added to add it or to explore how such lenses behave in photos.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:37:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2755203, 382986, 60862, '<td valign="top">I really, really like your concept.  And the selective desat and blurred hand help focus attention on the ball.  Unfortunately, the soft focus in the ball itself leaves me wanting to know more about what I''m seeing instead of grabbing my attention in a good way.  5.</td>', 'I really, really like your concept.  And the selective desat and blurred hand help focus attention on the ball.  Unfortunately, the soft focus in the ball itself leaves me wanting to know more about what I''m seeing instead of grabbing my attention in a good way.  5.', '2006-08-24 00:39:45.000000', NULL, 1),
